From 303f94e2dd498a482ab5c15584d225ea0d2f976e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:04:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkvdec: hevc: bound predicted short-term RPS sets

st_ref_pic_set_prediction() copies the use_delta_flag and
used_by_curr_pic bits of entries 0 to num_delta_pocs of the reference
set into two 16-entry stack arrays, and a predicted set can hold one
entry more than its reference set. The control validation accepts 16
entries in an explicit set, so the copy writes one byte past each stack
array and the predicted set its 17th entry past its 16-entry arrays,
and a chain of predicted sets writes further past the stack arrays and
the calculated sets. ITU-T H.265 7.4.8 bounds a set by
sps_max_dec_pic_buffering_minus1, at most 15 entries, and the hardware
table holds 15 entries per set.

A userspace V4L2 client that can open the RKVDEC m2m decoder can submit
an EXT_SPS_ST_RPS control whose predicted sets overflow these arrays.

Skip a predicted set whose reference set holds more than 15 entries,
as is done for a reference index out of range.

Fixes: c9a59dc2acc7 ("media: rkvdec: Add HEVC support for the VDPU381 variant")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-hevc-common.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-hevc-common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-hevc-common.c
@@ -223,6 +223,8 @@ static void st_ref_pic_set_prediction(st
 		   (rps_data->abs_delta_rps_minus1 + 1); /* 7-60 */
 
 	ref_rps = &calculated_rps_st_sets[ref_rps_idx];
+	if (ref_rps->num_delta_pocs >= ARRAY_SIZE(use_delta_flag))
+		return;
 
 	for (j = 0; j <= ref_rps->num_delta_pocs; j++) {
 		used_by_curr_pic_flag[j] = !!(rps_data->used_by_curr_pic & (1 << j));
